rkness a bit closer  the semi-transparent shape of the ship  itself starts to become visible link  won't be able to board the ship right  from the get-go as he'll just pass  through it unless he's in possession of  a special chart the ghost ship chart  once obtained instead of just passing  through link will instead be transported  to the ship's interior despite being one  of the most creepy and exciting  encounters in the game we barely know  anything about it there's no explanation  about its existence or why it continues  to haunt the seas whatsoever al exposure  suggests that it could have something to  do with the triforce depending on which  version of the game you play the ship  holds either a piece of the triforce of  courage or a treasure map leading to set  piece i'd say that in both instances  those on board were hiding it from the  rest of the world it's just that in the  hd version they removed the extra step  of having to go dig it up somewhere to  make the quest less cumbersome i think  it's definitely possible that being in  possession of a piece of the holy relic  somehow led to the ship and its crew  getting cursed even though the triforce  is generally seen as something positive  a divine gift historically it's also  driven certain people into a state of  madness greed betrayal and even outright  murder sometimes of their own comrades  so it's not unthinkable that even a  small piece of it can lead to some dire  consequences especially if its power was  never meant for them alternatively it  could have attracted some sort of  demonic presence similar to the ghost  ship from phantom hourglass which isn't  the same vessel as the two don't look  anything alike but is under the control  of bellum who is classified as a demon i  think it's all but certain that there is  a connection between the unfortunate  fate of those on board and the triforce  of courage because as soon as link  obtains it a blood-curdling screech can  be heard echoing from within 