 long the fabled hero  of time who they hoped would make a  return someday in his absence the boy  from outset island had to prove himself  to the gods and earned the triforce of  courage in the process to show that he  had what it takes to be a champion for  good and ultimately face ganondorf this  is in stark contrast to not only the  hero of time but also his descendant  from the child timeline the hero of  twilight from the moment they were born  they were predestined to become the  god's chosen hero especially in the case  of the hero of time who was a child of  prophecy both heroes have the triforce  symbol on the back of their hands  seemingly from birth and neither had to  prove their competence to the gods first  they were always destined for greatness  something that wasn't the case for link  in the wind waker he became a hero kind  of by accident really but what if he did  have a blood connection to a past hero  one who lived long before the events of  ocarina of time after all the hero of  time was by no means the first in line  there's at least three heroes that have  preceded him possibly even more like the  hero of men from minish cap's backstory  who we don't know much about and that is  exactly what azul suggests that link  from the wind waker could be a distant  relative of another hero specifically  link from diminish cap there's of course  the obvious similarities in their  physical appearance however this can  easily be chalked up to art style after  all there are similar looking heroes  from completely different timelines as  well now azul's reasoning for a blood  connection between these two is a lot  more subtle a tiny detail both literally  and figuratively that being the hero  shield according to link's grandmother  the shield is a family heirloom another  ceremonial artifact passed down from the  old days and the in-game description  states that it is said to have been  wielded by the legendary hero himself  it's implied that this is referring to  the hero of time as it's the only past  hero mentioned in the game's story  however this doesn't make much sense  when you really think about it the hero  of time utilized the hylian shield  during most of his adventure and  depending on your own fashion choice he  brandishes either the hylian shield or  the mirror shield at the moment he was  sent back in time now you could say that  well maybe the shield from the wind  waker is supposed to represent the  hylian shield again differences in art  style but if so why are these two  shields so radically different it's not  just a name that's different but the  size shape even the material doesn't  match in the slightest the hylian shield  is a sturdy high quality metal shield  whereas the hero shield is mostly made  of wood and overall pretty cheap looking  even tetra jokes about its quality  there's of course the difference in  color and perhaps most notably the size  the hero shield is incredibly small even  in the hands of a young child in fact it  seems to have been specifically made for  children compare this to the hylian  shield which is so big that as a child  link couldn't even hold it up like  normal and instead had to use it as a  turtle shell it's almost as big as he is  now that i think about it i'm pretty  sure the hylian shield traveled back  seven years with the hero of time right  to me the differences between the two  are simply too big to conclude that it's  the same shield but in a different art  style and why change the name if it  really was supposed to be one in the  same now there is a shield bearing the  same name present in the child timeline  the one link starts out with in majora's  mask while it's definitely smaller than  the hylian shield again the material and  color doesn't match we also have no idea  how exactly link got his hands on this  shield and more importantly he obtained  it in a completely different timeline as  a child long story short the hero of  time and hero of winds cannot be related  by blood and based on its physical  appearance and chronologically speaking  the hero shield is almost certainly not  the same as either of the two shields  the hero of time use it simply doesn't  match but like azul points out there is  a shield which does resemble the one  from the wind waker that being the tiny  shield from the minish cap which link is  seen carrying right there on the front  cover it's pretty much an exact match  right down to the color the size and the  decorations if this is indeed the same  shield it would be compelling evidence  that the heroes from minish cap and the  wind waker could share a blood  connection after all how did it end up  getting passed down in link's family for  all these countless ages the description  mentioned before never elaborates on  which hero used to wield it it doesn't  specifically say the hero of time so  could this instead be referencing a  different individual a hero who lived  long before the events of ocarina of  time and whose bloodline has survived  all the way up until now it would  explain why link despite being such a  young kid possesses so much strength and  courage seemingly for no reason other  than he's the hero of the story defying  the odds and slaying one of the most  dangerous individuals to walk this earth  all before even reaching adulthood and a  possible blood relation to the hero of  diminish could have given this unlikely  hero the edge he needed to fulfill his  goals whatever the case may be the idea  that this shield survived and was passed  down ever since the age of minish cap is  very compelling to me not because it's  magical or of exceptional quality  because frankly the opposite is true  it's a cheap simple tiny little shield  and there may have been many more like  it in its time but unlike the hylian  shield which was simply bought from a  random bazaar the hero shield has a  symbolic and sentimental value attached  to it it was a gift from one of the  earliest incarnations of princess zelda  herself an act of kindness and  generosity between two childhood friends  and one that ended up being  indispensable in link's quest to defeat  vati it's confirmed that the shield of  antiquity from spirit tracks is also the  very same one the hero of winds used on  his adventure kept safe and treasured by  his old friend nico so not only did it  survive from minish cap all the way up  until the wind waker but it even  persisted all the way up to the very end  of the adult timeline in a newly  established kingdom no less  this next theory is something i never  really thought about until now but  actually makes a lot of sense ocarina of  time first introduced the gerudo the  strong and proud women of the scorching  desert their biology somehow dictates  that almost everyone born into the tribe  is female with only one male being born  every 100 years during this age it was  custom for the male to become the  tribe's leader and the only male gerudo  we've met so far is of course the man  with the sinister plan ganondorf despite  being a familiar face in zelda lore the  gerudo only make an appearance in 5  games ganondorf not included of course  and in the case of majora's mask it's  debatable if these even are real gerudo  or just pirates with the same character  model the reason why the gerudo don't  appear very often in the timeline is  exactly because of their connection and  loyalty to ganondorf in every outcome  following ocarina of time ganondorf  suffers a temporary defeat in the chow  timeline he's captured and sealed inside  the twilight realm in the adult timeline  he's frozen at the bottom of the sea  along with the entire kingdom and in the  downfall timeline during the imprisoning  war he is banished to the dark world  formerly known as the sacred realm as  such the absence of the gerudo following  the timeline split makes sense in  twilight princess the desert is barren  and empty and it's implied that the  gerudo have either been killed or exiled  after ganondorf's capture they do show  up again in relatively large numbers in  four swords adventures this time as a  peaceful tribe who want nothing to do  with ganondorf so i'm inclined to  believe that some did manage to escape  persecution back then in the adult  timeline they are never seen again in  any of the games which leads me to  believe that they probably didn't  survive past the great flood when it  comes to the downfall timeline their  fate is equally uncertain the same type  of scenarios are possible of course they  could have been killed in the  imprisoning war or exiled the only  appearance of gerudo beside ganon are  kaume and kotake in orkov ages and  seasons which don't even take place in  hyrule aside from them it does seem to  suggest that the rest of the tribe may  not have survived this outcome either  whatever happened before the events of a  link to the past their presence name and  influence are all but a distant memory  seemingly wiped from the history books  brick colby has a logical yet kind of  disturbing explanation as to why the  gerudo are barely seen again in this  timeline one that emphasizes the sheer  brutality of ganondorf as a leader if we  study the backstory of a link to the  past from the instruction manual it says  that at some point the doors to the  sacred realm the resting place of the  triforce at the time were breached by a  gang of thieves and that ganon fought  his way past his own followers  vanquishing them and eventually standing  triumphant with blood-stained hands  claiming the triforce as his prize he  allegedly even made his wish right then  and there the first and only time ganon  has succeeded in getting his wish  granted by the triforce the band of  thieves described here fits the profile  of the gerudo as they are referred to as  search in ocarina of time now this  backstory is a bit outdated as it was  written long before the zelda team had a  solid grasp on if and how