k to  hyrule after he succeeds either the  triforce can only provide a one-way  ticket or it's just being a dick but  that's beside the point either way after  concluding his quest in these respective  lands he would have had to find a way  back to hyrule on his own thus he set  sail for hyrule but before making it to  his final destination his vessel gets  hit by lightning and the story of link's  awakening picks up again by no means  perfect but i prefer not having to  imagine a quest that happens off screen  over a small inconsistency in the  backstory we of course have to remember  that a link to the past and link's  awakening were written long before the  oracle games not only that but the  oracle games were made by capcom so i  can forgive a few discrepancies in the  storytelling here and with a little bit  of creativity we can make this work yes  link technically didn't set out on a  journey on his own and was instead  summoned by the triforce but as we can  see in the intro he did travel to the  castle on horseback willingly to seek  audience with it so we can still kind of  consider this a personal quest either  way seeing as breath wild has kind of  wiped the slate clean it's unlikely that  the timeline will ever get updated and  even if it does they probably won't  bother with such an insignificant detail  but to me the old chronology of these  four games will always make more sense  to me unless someone comes up with a  solid theory that convinces me otherwise  and that concludes part 1 of your zelda  theories part 2 and 3 will follow soon  however i will spread them out a bit  across the rest of the year in between  other videos i have a lot more subjects  and ideas i really want to get to and i  don't want to hold these back for too  long i like mixing things up and variety  is a big part of my enjoyment as a  creator once again i cannot thank you  all enough for the support and for  getting the channel this far as always a  huge thanks goes to my mods